<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Background of the MISSA TV 360 PLUS top navigation strip (NAV-01, THEME-01, A11Y-01).

    AUDIT H1 (2026-11-05, Option 1): a flat surface with a single brand accent, so the
    bar disappears behind its content instead of reading as a decorative banner.

    What changed and why: the old "horizon ambre / émeraude" glows carried
    android:alpha="0.14" on their <item>. LayerDrawableItem declares no `alpha`
    attribute (checked against AOSP's declare-styleable), so the attribute was
    silently ignored and both glows painted at full intensity (#FFC12E and #2FD37A).
    The result was a gold block on the left and an emerald one on the right, and the
    wordmark - drawn in ?attr/missaAccentPrimary - was lost on the gold.

    Brand colour budget from now on:
      - amber   : the wordmark and the selected pill only
      - emerald : the TV focus ring and the "360+" badge only
      - red     : LIVE only
    No decorative emerald hairline at the bottom of the bar any more: the separator
    uses the same subtle stroke as the cards, so light themes stay correct.

    Anti-banding (THEME-06): the sheen is a short, low-alpha ramp and the zero-mean
    dither tile is kept so 8-bit TV panels still show no steps.
    HEADER-01 (2026-11-04): the tile MUST stay 32x32. A <bitmap> child passes its
    intrinsic size to LayerDrawable.getMinimumHeight(), and the ribbon is a
    wrap_content LinearLayout, so the 128x128 tile that shipped with the anti-banding
    fix pinned the whole header to 128px: the pill row stayed at the top and ~65px of
    dead background appeared underneath it, and no layout height change had any
    visible effect.

    The height of the ribbon is NOT defined here and must not be (62dp, accepted).
-->
<layer-list xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

    <!-- 1. Theme-aware base (black on AMOLED, #111111 on dark, light grey on light themes) -->
    <item>
        <shape android:shape="rectangle">
            <solid android:color="?attr/primaryBlackBackground" />
        </shape>
    </item>

    <!-- 2. Vertical sheen, 4% white: lifts the bar off the void without a colour cast -->
    <item>
        <shape android:shape="rectangle">
            <gradient
                android:angle="270"
                android:endColor="#00FFFFFF"
                android:startColor="#0AFFFFFF" />
        </shape>
    </item>

    <!-- 3. Zero-mean dither tile: removes the 8-bit steps of the sheen above (THEME-06) -->
    <item>
        <bitmap
            android:src="@drawable/missa_dither_noise"
            android:tileMode="repeat" />
    </item>

    <!-- 4. Separation hairline: the theme's subtle stroke, the one the cards already use -->
    <item
        android:gravity="bottom"
        android:height="1dp">
        <shape android:shape="rectangle">
            <solid android:color="?attr/missaStrokeSubtle" />
        </shape>
    </item>

</layer-list>
